1671
01:59:08.145 --> 01:59:12.005
<i>ALMOST ALL OF THE
300,000 TROOPS AT DUNKIRK</i>

1672
01:59:12.276 --> 01:59:16.526
<i>WERE CARRIED HOME
BY WINSTON'S CIVILIAN FLEET</i>

1673
01:59:17.451 --> 01:59:22.363
<i>NEVILLE CHAMBERLAIN DIED SIX MONTHS LATER</i>

1674
01:59:23.531 --> 01:59:26.581
<i>VISCOUNT HALIFAX WAS SOON
REMOVED BY WINSTON</i>

1675
01:59:26.681 --> 01:59:29.447
<i>FROM THE WAR CABINET
AND SENT TO WASHINGTON</i>

1676
01:59:30.431 --> 01:59:31.914
<i>ON MAY 8, FIVE YEARS LATER,</i>

1677
01:59:32.014 --> 01:59:35.133
<i>BRITAIN AND ITS ALLIES
WOULD DECLARE VICTORY</i>

1678
01:59:35.233 --> 01:59:40.084
<i>LATER THAT YEAR, WINSTON WAS VOTED OUT
OF OFFICE IN THE GENERAL ELECTION</i>

1679
01:59:41.202 --> 01:59:44.114
<i>"SUCCESS IS NOT FINAL,
FAILURE IS NOT FATAL.</i>

1680
01:59:44.214 --> 01:59:46.646
<i>IT IS THE COURAGE
TO CONTINUE THAT COUNTS."</i>

1681
01:59:46.746 --> 01:59:47.986
<i>WINSTON CHURCHILL</i>
